Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:28:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] windows: rebase refuses a diff file that is not sparse

rebase-snap and snapshot-editor edit-memory rebase copy a diff file's
data over the base and skip its holes. On Linux a file extended by
set_len, or written past a gap, has holes there; on Windows only a file
marked sparse does, and any other has allocated zeros, which SEEK_DATA
rightly reports as data. Given such a file, both tools copied its zeros
over the base and exited 0 (measured: 979244 of 1048576 base bytes
zeroed). Firecracker's own diff snapshots are sparse (keep_holes), but
every ordinary copy (Copy-Item, copy, xcopy, robocopy, esentutl)
drops the attribute and allocates the file.

So on Windows both tools refuse a diff file with data that is not
sparse, before writing anything (vmm_sys_util::seek_hole::holes_kept):
the base is left as it was. A dense file marked sparse afterwards is
still copied whole, as on Linux a diff file that lost its holes is:
neither can tell a lost hole from a page of zeros.

Upstream's unit tests that make holes with set_len in a file that is not
sparse (rebase-snap's test_rebase, test_rebase_corner_cases;
snapshot-editor's test_rebase, test_rebase_empty_diff,
test_rebase_full_diff) now fail on Windows with that refusal, where they
failed with a corrupted base before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/rebase-snap/src/main.rs            | 3 +++
 src/snapshot-editor/src/edit_memory.rs | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/rebase-snap/src/main.rs b/src/rebase-snap/src/main.rs
index 3950dca27ba7a64e5b7ca88f982198eb209ee022..3690da6c721f7e485b7509f9474dda3bb5b38687 100644
--- a/src/rebase-snap/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/rebase-snap/src/main.rs
@@ -87,6 +87,9 @@ fn get_files(args: &Arguments) -> Result<(File, File), FileError> {
 }
 
 fn rebase(base_file: &mut File, diff_file: &mut File) -> Result<(), FileError> {
+    // wick: on Windows only a sparse file has holes; any other would be copied whole.
+    #[cfg(windows)]
+    vmm_sys_util::seek_hole::holes_kept(diff_file).map_err(FileError::InvalidDiffFile)?;
     let mut cursor: u64 = 0;
     while let Some(block_start) = diff_file.seek_data(cursor).map_err(FileError::SeekData)? {
         cursor = block_start;
